# Several axes (A4, R1). Rotate with a multi-axis subscript turns each
# listed axis; a list of amounts gives every combination, one leading
# result axis per listed axis. Reduce and scan with several axes work
# on each listed axis in turn: `'+ r_/_12` reduces axis 1 and then the
# new axis 1 (the original axis 2).
== SOURCE
b := 3 3 r_eshape 1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8 9
1 o_-_12 b
s_hape -1 0 1 o_-_12 b
s_hape -1 0 1 o_-_2 b
-1 0 1 o_-_1 1 2 3
'+ r_/_12 -1 0 1 o_-_12 b
'+ r_/_12 b
'+ r_/_21 b
'+ s_\_12 b
'- r_/_12 2 2 r_eshape 10 1 2 3
